מסדירים - חלוקת התנ"ך לסדרים
Masdirim - the Tanakh by the Jewish division into sedarim
https://www.masdirim.org · https://github.com/bambiker/sdarim

Everyone may take from this project whatever they want, for any purpose, also commercial, as long as
they say where they took it from, so others can reach the source and check it for updates:

    מקור: מסדירים, https://www.masdirim.org

In detail:

1. The code (the .js, .py, .mjs, .html and .css files) is under the MIT License below.

2. The data and the texts written for the site (sdarim.json, API/, calendar/parashot.json, the generated
   pages seder/, perek/, parasha/, book/, and the site's own texts) are under the Creative Commons
   Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ :
   you may copy, change and share them for any purpose, if you give credit to Masdirim
   (https://www.masdirim.org), link to the license, and say if you changed them.

3. Files that come from others keep their own licenses, which go with them:
   - commentary/ : the commentaries, from Sefaria's public export; the edition and license of each
     commentator and book are in commentary/sources.json (public domain, CC0, CC-BY or CC-BY-SA).
   - calendar/haftarot.json : the haftarot and the readings of the festivals, from @hebcal/leyning
     (BSD 2-Clause License, https://github.com/hebcal/hebcal-leyning).
   - API/letters.json and API/sections.json : the big, small and raised letters, and the open and closed
     sections, from "Miqra according to the Masorah" (Sefaria, CC BY-SA 4.0).
   - API/songs.json : the layout of the songs (שירות), from MAM-parsed, "Miqra according to the Masorah"
     (https://github.com/bdenckla/MAM-basics, CC BY-SA 4.0).

